# Server Functions | TanStack Start Solid Docs
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-03-29, [Read more](https://tanstack.com/start/v0/docs/framework/solid/server-functions)

Server functions are defined with the createServerFn function, from the @tanstack/solid-start package.
This function takes an optional options argument for specifying configuration like the HTTP method and response type, and allows you to chain off the result to define things like the body of the server function, input validation, middleware, etc.
Here's a simple example:
...
import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'
export const getServerTime = createServerFn().handler(async () => {
// Wait for 1 second
await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000))
// Return the current time
return new Date().toISOString()
})
...
import { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'
export const getData = createServerFn({
method: 'GET', // HTTP method to use
response: 'data', // Response handling mode
}).handler(async () => {
// Function implementation
})
...
})
